\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{booktabs}
\begin{document}
\section{Measurements}
We measured density and modulus for three alloys. The stiffness is $k = E^{2}_{eff} A / L$ for the equivalent spring model.
\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{Measured alloy properties}
\begin{tabular}{lcc}
\toprule
Sample & Density (g/cm$^3$) & Modulus (GPa) \\
\midrule
A1 & 2.70 & 69 \\
B2 & 7.85 & 210 & \\
C3 & 8.96 & 117 \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}
The effective exponent uses $E^{2}^{eff}$ as a shorthand in the fitting script.
The variable sample_id in the export script holds the batch identifier.
\end{document}

